arm64: dts: allwinner: h713: describe the codec's I2S window

The codec node has always carried a note that the stock device tree
gives it a second reg range at 0x02031000, 0x7c long, and that nobody
knew what it was. It is the I2S receiver that feeds the DAC: the
register names and the length both come out of the stock kernel's
i2s_reg_labels table @0xc149ce98 and sunxi_i2s_regmap_config
@0xc0ee8a54 (S25 §1), and the path through it was measured on the
board on 08.09.2026, carrying HDMI audio from the MSP DSP to the
speaker (S16 20:30).

Name both ranges, because the driver asks for the second one by name
and has to be able to tell an old device tree apart from a new one.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -782,18 +782,24 @@
 			 * its own DAI and card, so those two nodes have no
 			 * mainline equivalent.
 			 *
+			 * The second reg range is the I2S receiver that feeds
+			 * the DAC: the vendor's own register names for it, and
+			 * its length, come out of the stock kernel's
+			 * i2s_reg_labels table and sunxi_i2s_regmap_config.
+			 * It is what carries the decoded HDMI audio from the
+			 * audio DSP to the speaker.
+			 *
 			 * Values taken from the stock DTB and kept here because
 			 * they are measured, not guessed:
-			 *   second reg range 0x02031000 len 0x7c, probably the
-			 *     analog block -- H616 needs only one range, so try
-			 *     one first
 			 *   speaker_vol 0x1a, digital_vol 0x00, headphone unused
 			 *   pa_level 1 (active high), pa_msleep_time 160 ms
 			 *   stock also lists a pll_tvfe clock on the codec,
 			 *     which is unexplained -- deliberately not copied
 			 */
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h713-codec";
-			reg = <0x02030000 0x32c>;
+			reg = <0x02030000 0x32c>,
+			      <0x02031000 0x7c>;
+			reg-names = "codec", "i2s";
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 25 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_AUDIO_CODEC>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_AUDIO_CODEC_DAC>;
